    "text": "<p>The speed of light in media <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively. A ray of light enters from the medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;at an incident angle<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>. If the ray suffers total internal reflection, then</p>",
